   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 2361848,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 418619,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > be a natural number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a865bb129be512b7d58dee72870efe97a27696c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\ldots , x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"11\" > further natural numbers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > and such that the least common multiple of any two of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > numbers is greater than <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that the sum of the reciprocals of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > numbers is always less than <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" >:</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c166ec5cd8f822214d10b661d558f8d83baadccf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum^n_{i=1} \\frac{1}{x_i} &lt; 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"85\" height=\"48\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $N$ be a natural number and $x_1, \\ldots , x_n$ further natural numbers less than $N$ and such that the least common multiple of any two of these $n$ numbers is greater than $N$. Prove that the sum of the reciprocals of these $n$ numbers is always less than $2$: $\\sum^n_{i=1} \\frac{1}{x_i} < 2.$",
    "username": "orl",
    "post_number": 1,
