    "topic_id": 17330,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" > from the reals to the reals such that<br>\n<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4e0d6580d9d3d6a627e39837edb3d1943d4596.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(f(x)+y\\right)=2x+f\\left(f(y)-x\\right)\\]\"  width=\"254\" height=\"18\" ><br>\n<br>\nfor all real <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Find all functions $f$ from the reals to the reals such that\r\n\r\n\\[f\\left(f(x)+y\\right)=2x+f\\left(f(y)-x\\right)\\]\r\n\r\nfor all real $x,y$.",
